      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That \"epilogue\" feeling is heavy, and it's understandable that waiting for life to resume can make you feel like you've already been written out. But your story isn't over—you're not just taking up space, you're still the author of what happens next, even if the chapters are slower. Your kids might not say it, but your presence is a quiet anchor in their lives, not a burden. If movement feels impossible, maybe you can start with one tiny plot twist—a new book, a short call to an old friend, or simply noticing one small beautiful thing today. You are still here, and that still matters.",
